---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteBasePath } from '../../paths';

const site = 'https://ysskrishna.github.io/google-sheets-text-power-tools';
const pageUrl = `${site}/how-to/change-case.html`;
const screenshotUrl = `${site}/assets/store_screenshots/1.jpg`;

const ldJson = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'WebSite',
      '@id': `${site}/#website`,
      name: 'Text Power Tools',
      url: `${site}/`,
    },
    {
      '@type': 'HowTo',
      '@id': `${pageUrl}#howto`,
      name: 'How to change case in Google Sheets',
      description:
        'Change the case of selected cells in Google Sheets in one click with Text Power Tools, without nesting UPPER, LOWER, or PROPER formulas.',
      url: pageUrl,
      inLanguage: 'en',
      tool: { '@type': 'HowToTool', name: 'Text Power Tools add-on for Google Sheets' },
      step: [
        {
          '@type': 'HowToStep',
          position: 1,
          name: 'Select the cells',
          text: 'Select the cells whose text you want to change.',
        },
        {
          '@type': 'HowToStep',
          position: 2,
          name: 'Open the sidebar',
          text: 'Open the Text Power Tools menu and choose Start. The sidebar opens on the Case tab.',
        },
        {
          '@type': 'HowToStep',
          position: 3,
          name: 'Click a case',
          text: 'Click the case you want. Each button applies its change to the selected cells right away.',
        },
      ],
    },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How to change case in Google Sheets"
  description="Change the case of cells in Google Sheets in one click with Text Power Tools, without nesting UPPER, LOWER, and PROPER formulas."
  canonical={pageUrl}
  navKey="how-to-change-case"
  mainClass="site-main--inner"
  ogTitle="How to change case in Google Sheets"
  ogDescription="Change text case in Google Sheets in one click, without nesting UPPER, LOWER, or PROPER formulas."
  ogUrl={pageUrl}
  ogImage={screenshotUrl}
  twitterCard="summary_large_image"
  twitterImage={screenshotUrl}
  ldJson={ldJson}
>
  <h1 class="page-title">How to change case in Google Sheets</h1>

  <p>
    Changing text case with formulas usually means nesting <code>UPPER</code>, <code>LOWER</code>, and
    <code>PROPER</code> together, and it gets harder for sentence case or code styles such as camelCase and
    snake_case. Text Power Tools applies these changes to the cells you select, one click at a time.
  </p>

  <h2>Steps</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Select the cells whose text you want to change.</li>
    <li>Open the <strong>Text Power Tools</strong> menu and choose <strong>Start</strong>. The sidebar opens on the <strong>Case</strong> tab.</li>
    <li>
      Click the case you want. Each button applies its change to the selected cells right away, so there is no
      Apply button. Common options are Sentence case, Capitalized Case, lower case, UPPER CASE, and iNVERT cASE.
      Advanced options include kebab-case, hyphen-case, dot.case, camelCase, PascalCase, snake_case,
      SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE, SCREAMING-KEBAB-CASE, and AlTeRnAtInG cAsE.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <figure class="how-to-figure">
    <img
      src={`${siteBasePath}assets/store_screenshots/1.jpg`}
      alt="Text Power Tools sidebar showing the Case tab with Common and Advanced case options"
      width="1080"
      height="1920"
      loading="lazy"
    />
    <figcaption>The Case tab in the Text Power Tools sidebar.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .how-to-figure {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    max-width: 22rem;
  }

  .how-to-figure img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
</style>
